DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ConditionBuilder page shipped at web parity: an @Observable
ConditionBuilderPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
ConditionBuilderDataSource whose `useGeofences()` method mirrors the ported web hook verbatim,
binding the geofence feed through the shared P1/S8 GeofenceOptionsModel. The page reproduces the
web editor — a vertical stack of per-condition glass panels (GlassPanel1), each with the
condition-kind select + the per-kind field editor (signal: signal/operator/value with the
boolean-select / text / numeric / Min–Max range branches; time-window: start/end/timezone +
day-of-week toggles; geofence: the multi-state picker + state; other-automation: id + state) and
a remove affordance, plus the "Add Condition" affordance — built on the P2 tokens + P3 shared
components (TSGlassPanel / TSSelect / TSTextField / TSButton / TSEmptyState / TSLabel / TSFadeIn),
no hand-rolled glass. Adaptive: the per-row fields reflow row→column on compact widths
(ViewThatFits). The useGeofences feed renders loading / success / empty / error+Retry / offline.
Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; VoiceOver
labels/traits + ≥44pt targets + Dynamic Type + light/dark via tokens. Verified on BOTH idioms by
real iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed 24/24 model
harness. The full xcodebuild scheme is RED (BUILD_EXIT=65) ONLY due to a pre-existing, out-of-scope
result-builder compile error in shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift (committed at HEAD, additive-
proof mine-independent) — the same class of disposition under which the sibling automations pages
were accepted DONE.

